  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` according to `docs/SPEC.md`. `npm test` passes, with 4 tests passing and 0 failing.\n\nI added `test/satisfies.test.js`. It has about 100 cases covering the spec's examples (the X-range, tilde, caret and hyphen tables, and the prerelease rules) and a set of invalid inputs that must return `false`.\n\nWhere the spec was silent, I made these calls:\n- `1.x.3` is invalid, because a wildcard can't be followed by a concrete number.\n- A prerelease on a partial version such as `1.2-beta` is invalid.\n- `~ 1.2.3` and `^ 1.2.3` are invalid, because the spec only allows a space after `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` and `=`.\n- An empty set in a range such as `1.0.0 ||` matches any version.\n- A numeric prerelease identifier with a leading zero is accepted, since the spec only bans leading zeros in `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`.\n- `>*` and `<*` match nothing.\n\nIf you want any of those handled differently, say which.",
